1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:03,000
Damn it! You're kidding me!

2
00:00:03,280 --> 00:00:05,520
This wall wasn't here last time! What gives?

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:07,880
Another earthquake?

4
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:10,040
That's not what that was.

5
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:12,780
The dungeon is moving and changing its shape.

6
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:15,260
I bet that mage is doing it.

7
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:18,060
He's probably being cautious about us.

8
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:22,340
Does that mean we'll be wandering around this place in circles till we die?

9
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:25,180
Guess I've got to get a bit reckless.

10
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:26,820
Just wait here!

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,600
The coast is clear.

12
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:41,280
Looks like climbing the wall might not be such a great idea.

13
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:44,040
Well, it's time to start walking then.

14
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:49,880
I don't know if anyone else is getting this feeling, but...

15
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,580
It's like the town is getting livelier.

16
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:56,820
With the Red Dragon dead, the monsters hiding from it are surfacing.

17
00:00:57,180 --> 00:00:59,700
This floor originally had lots of monsters.

18
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:02,360
Us avoiding them with sheer good love.

19
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:07,340
Whoa, are you guys all right?

20
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:09,920
Hmm, so unhealthy.

21
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:14,380
We've been walking non-stop and haven't had a decent meal since eating the dragon.

22
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,940
If I had to guess Laios' age...

23
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:20,600
Well, I can't really tell if he's young or old simply by looking.

24
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:24,380
But Chilchuk and Marcel are definitely still growing.

25
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:25,360
Come on.

26
00:01:25,360 --> 00:01:30,660
I'm overwhelmed with shame that I can't provide a hearty meal at such an important time in their lives.

27
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,200
I must feed them.

28
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:33,960
The young'uns must be fed.

29
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:35,860
And I have to feed them!

30
00:01:36,860 --> 00:01:39,040
Hmm, I smell something kind of sweet.

31
00:01:39,460 --> 00:01:40,380
Something you can eat?

32
00:01:40,380 --> 00:01:43,680
No, it's more like a floral scent.

33
00:01:44,420 --> 00:01:47,220
Wherever flowers are blooming, there's sure to be some water.

34
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:49,420
It's all up to you, Chilchuk.

35
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:50,200
I'm on it!

36
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:57,300
Is this place some kind of graveyard?

37
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:02,340
Wait, what's that over there?

38
00:02:08,340 --> 00:02:09,300
Don't look!

39
00:02:12,060 --> 00:02:13,920
Oh, excuse us.

40
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:15,680
Hey, Senshi, let go!

41
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:19,520
Get back, Senshi!

42
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:25,700
What's that?

43
00:02:26,260 --> 00:02:27,080
Arm yourselves!

44
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:29,160
These things aren't humans.

45
00:02:29,740 --> 00:02:31,680
They're dry-head flowers.

46
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:33,760
Then there's dust in the air is.

47
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,920
It's not dust at all.

48
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:41,220
Once inhaled, these microparticles cling to the respiratory system's mucous membrane.

49
00:02:42,020 --> 00:02:45,400
The body recognizes these particles and labels them as harmful.

50
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:50,220
Then activates its immune system and quickly tries to dispel them.

51
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:52,000
Simply put,

52
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:56,280
it's hay fever.

53
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:56,960
Ew!

54
00:02:57,380 --> 00:02:58,520
This is so gross!

55
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:02,020
Try its pollen!

56
00:03:02,220 --> 00:03:02,720
No way!

57
00:03:03,420 --> 00:03:03,860
Crap!

58
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:05,180
Don't inhale it!

59
00:03:09,820 --> 00:03:11,140
This is bad!

60
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:12,740
I can't stop crying!

61
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:12,900
I can't stop crying!

62
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:18,760
Come on, Senshi!

63
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:20,100
You gotta stand up!

64
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:21,600
Loyal!

65
00:03:21,740 --> 00:03:23,060
I can't escape!

66
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:24,260
Where are you?

67
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:26,340
My eyes!

68
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:30,100
Senshi, reach forward!

69
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:31,220
On my signal,

70
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:33,600
I want you to swing that sword behind you!

71
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:34,680
Ready?

72
00:03:35,740 --> 00:03:36,680
And...

73
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:37,960
Swing!

74
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:47,620
My eyes are suddenly getting itchy!

75
00:03:48,220 --> 00:03:49,880
My vision is...

76
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:58,620
Run, Senshi!

77
00:03:58,860 --> 00:03:59,220
No!

78
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:02,740
It's my job to stay here and protect all the young'uns from harm!

79
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:04,300
What are you talking about?

80
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:05,000
Jilchuk!

81
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:06,960
I'm gonna need you to be my eyes!

82
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:07,680
Tau!

83
00:04:07,740 --> 00:04:08,840
I can't see anything!

84
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:12,020
Your five senses are better than most, aren't they?

85
00:04:13,580 --> 00:04:14,060
Smell.

86
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:15,180
No.

87
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:17,420
The scent of the pollen is too strong.

88
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:19,240
Sound.

89
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:22,900
Senshi's sneezing is too loud!

90
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:25,840
I can't trust my sight, smell, or hearing right now.

91
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:27,060
I know!

92
00:04:27,740 --> 00:04:28,600
It's the wind!

93
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:33,060
It thought you'd sneeze and move to your back right!

94
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:35,400
Swing up in that direction, Senshi!

95
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:45,440
Ken-skei...

96
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:49,040
It completely snapped in two.

97
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:52,620
I need to repair it and feed it some mana quickly or it'll die.

98
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:56,980
And after it took me so many years to get it to grow this much...

99
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:58,100
Hmm?

100
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,120
This...

101
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:02,880
This whole area is safe!

102
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:03,860
You're such a liar!

103
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:06,800
You guys fought against dryad flowers?

104
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:09,240
That must have been rough.

105
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:11,240
So they were flower monsters, huh?

106
00:05:11,960 --> 00:05:14,540
And here I was thinking they were human men and women.

107
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:17,260
The male and female part was right.

108
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:18,700
Dryads are unisexual.

109
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:19,440
Oh!

110
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:20,580
Hang on a minute!

111
00:05:21,340 --> 00:05:22,640
He's doing it again.

112
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:25,060
Think we should knock him out to stop him this time?

113
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:28,800
I feel like we've gotten to a point where we can't be picky anymore.

114
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:31,140
I found myself having thoughts like,

115
00:05:31,260 --> 00:05:33,380
so what if the flower is shaped like a human?

116
00:05:34,220 --> 00:05:34,660
Marcy.

117
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:34,940
Ah!

118
00:05:34,940 --> 00:05:35,040
Ah!

119
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:35,440
Ah!

120
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:35,540
Ah!

121
00:05:35,540 --> 00:05:35,660
Ah!

122
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:35,680
Ah!

123
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:35,760
Ah!

124
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:37,940
Found some!

125
00:05:38,940 --> 00:05:40,900
Beautiful dryad fruit!

126
00:05:41,900 --> 00:05:44,120
How do I reverse time?

127
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:44,700
Cut it out!

128
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:46,900
Don't casually look for scary-sounding spells!

129
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:48,740
Your black magic jokes aren't funny,

130
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:50,040
so seriously stop!

131
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:54,600
I didn't see a lick of pollen come out of this last dryad I cut down.

132
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:56,940
The female flower, then.

133
00:05:57,700 --> 00:05:58,780
Before pollination,

134
00:05:59,140 --> 00:06:01,180
flowers care for and protect the other fruit.

135
00:06:02,860 --> 00:06:05,160
Hey, this thing kinda looks like fruit, too.

136
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:06,160
Yeah, good find.

137
00:06:06,460 --> 00:06:07,560
Those are flower buds.

138
00:06:07,820 --> 00:06:09,860
They're what eventually becomes the dryad flower.

139
00:06:09,860 --> 00:06:13,960
They look tasty and much easier to eat than the stuff you're carrying.

140
00:06:14,320 --> 00:06:15,600
What's the worst that could happen?

141
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:17,000
Let's grab a few.

142
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:21,340
Don't pluck too many of them.

143
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:21,880
Got it?

144
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:25,040
Understood.

145
00:06:26,180 --> 00:06:26,580
Whoa!

146
00:06:26,940 --> 00:06:28,280
There are mandrakes growing here.

147
00:06:28,580 --> 00:06:29,660
There's no dog around,

148
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:31,760
so we'll just have to chop off their heads, okay?

149
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:32,240
Hmm.

150
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:33,800
Seriously, Chill Chuck?

151
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:35,220
Can you drop that already?

152
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:37,120
Hmm.

153
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:40,260
A pretty good harvest, if I say so myself.

154
00:06:40,580 --> 00:06:41,740
I'm glad I thought ahead

155
00:06:41,740 --> 00:06:43,860
and asked to borrow this axe from those orcs.

156
00:06:44,020 --> 00:06:44,420
Chee!

157
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:47,920
Put the chopped ingredients into a pot with water

158
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:49,080
and bring to a boil.

159
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:50,960
When they become soft,

160
00:06:51,140 --> 00:06:52,160
remove them from the heat

161
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:54,300
and give them a good mashing in the pot.

162
00:06:55,300 --> 00:06:56,840
Once it becomes paste-like,

163
00:06:57,060 --> 00:07:00,040
add some more water along with your preferred seasonings.

164
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:01,260
Hmm.

165
00:07:01,260 --> 00:07:01,460
Hmm.

166
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:07,700
It already smells good.

167
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:09,320
In that case,

168
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:11,520
lightly fry it in some butter

169
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:13,100
and then add in some mushrooms.

170
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:16,340
Pour a little melted cheese over the top

171
00:07:16,340 --> 00:07:18,580
and it's ready.

172
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:23,360
Why'd you put it in that thing?

173
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:25,240
I figured it might give you some help

174
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:26,440
with replenishing your mana.

175
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:28,180
You can have good intentions,

176
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:30,040
but that doesn't make doing it any better.

177
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:31,740
I'll still eat it, though.

178
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:34,280
It's sweet!

179
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:36,020
There's a floral fragrance,

180
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:37,460
and despite it being dense,

181
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:38,740
it melts in your mouth.

182
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:40,240
I love this.

183
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:42,860
That's kind of horrifying.

184
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:50,100
The acidity of the cheese works well.

185
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:52,460
I personally like how there's a slight bitterness.

186
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:55,080
So now what?

187
00:07:55,320 --> 00:07:57,020
How do we escape from this place?

188
00:07:57,360 --> 00:07:59,120
What if we end up stuck in here forever?

189
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:01,560
Sealing the path to the surface

190
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:02,840
will cut the flow of magic,

191
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:05,880
so I highly doubt he'd try to keep us here indefinitely.

192
00:08:06,580 --> 00:08:08,460
Which means there has to be a way out.

193
00:08:08,460 --> 00:08:11,720
Do you think there's any kind of logic

194
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:12,800
to the dungeon changes?

195
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:14,180
That's it!

196
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:16,560
I'll record the frequency of the earthquakes on the map.

197
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:18,640
I'm starting to think this might work out.

198
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:20,620
It's a lot easier to feel optimistic

199
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:22,120
when your stomach's full, huh?

200
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:28,580
My body's all nice and toasty now.

201
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:30,920
Seems like some of my mana is back, too.

202
00:08:31,540 --> 00:08:34,100
Laios, Senshi, we should get your wounds healed up.

203
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:36,340
You don't need to push yourself this soon.

204
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:37,360
I'm not healing.

205
00:08:38,160 --> 00:08:38,900
You are.

206
00:08:39,280 --> 00:08:40,600
You really need to step up.

207
00:08:41,860 --> 00:08:43,880
It's time for me to teach you magic.

208
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:46,340
I won't be able to protect everybody

209
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:48,120
from the Mad Mage all by myself.

210
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:51,220
If you can learn healing and abjuration magic,

211
00:08:51,420 --> 00:08:52,860
it'll make things easier.

212
00:08:53,620 --> 00:08:55,440
Fallon taught you the basics, didn't she?

213
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:56,740
More or less.

214
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:59,620
She actually specialized in the Gnome magic system,

215
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:01,660
which is a bit different from the magic system

216
00:09:01,660 --> 00:09:02,800
I learned to use.

217
00:09:03,020 --> 00:09:05,700
But the roots are similar, so it should be okay.

218
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,000
I'll drum it into your head fast, I swear.

219
00:09:10,560 --> 00:09:11,560
Let's do this.

220
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:12,660
And get stronger.

221
00:09:12,660 --> 00:09:18,400
They're too optimistic about this.

222
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:21,740
And that's exactly how young people should be.

223
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:25,900
Can you stop treating me like a child already, Senshi?

224
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:27,620
I'm so tired of it!

225
00:09:27,820 --> 00:09:30,500
Why'd you even cover my eyes in front of those dryads anyway?

226
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:32,620
I mean, you saved me, but still!

227
00:09:33,620 --> 00:09:34,420
I see.

228
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:36,080
Well, Chilchuk,

229
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:39,220
you said before that your old man passed away, didn't you?

230
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:41,540
Yeah, what about it?

231
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:42,060
Hmm.

232
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:44,640
Now is as good a time as any.

233
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:46,820
I'll teach you what you need to know.

234
00:09:47,780 --> 00:09:49,200
Go and take a seat right there.

235
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:52,080
You're probably at the age

236
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:54,780
where you're gonna start showing interest in certain things,

237
00:09:55,100 --> 00:09:57,400
so you're gonna need to have some good knowledge about them.

238
00:09:57,920 --> 00:09:58,840
What's that mean?

239
00:09:59,040 --> 00:10:02,200
Let's just say that humans also have a stamen and pistol.

240
00:10:04,360 --> 00:10:05,880
Wrong! Do it again!

241
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:07,260
Are you listening?

242
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:12,720
And so their lessons continued on well into the night.

243
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:16,260
Come on, do it.

244
00:10:22,540 --> 00:10:23,440
The hell?

245
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:27,380
I thought touching it softly might be kind of weird.

246
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:29,540
That's not the point at all, so get over it!

247
00:10:29,900 --> 00:10:30,980
Give me your left hand.

248
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:34,020
See?

249
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:35,960
Something like this is fine.

250
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:40,520
Your magic won't improve if things like this embarrass you.

251
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:41,640
Come on, focus!

252
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:45,860
You need to become aware of the mana that flows within your body.

253
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:47,720
It's like the Venus system.

254
00:10:48,380 --> 00:10:50,540
Link that flow with the palm of your hand,

255
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:54,640
from the very top of your head and all the way down to my toes.

256
00:10:55,260 --> 00:10:56,360
Match to my breathing,

257
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:58,540
my body temp and pulse.

258
00:10:59,060 --> 00:11:01,060
When you feel like you have the rhythm down,

259
00:11:01,340 --> 00:11:02,280
repeat after me.

260
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:16,020
It itches!

261
00:11:17,620 --> 00:11:18,820
It's so itchy!

262
00:11:19,520 --> 00:11:20,640
Are you all right?

263
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:21,440
What the?

264
00:11:21,820 --> 00:11:23,340
The scap just came off.

265
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:25,860
Wow, you actually did it!

266
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:27,040
Good job, Lyos!

267
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:28,520
Are you sure about that?

268
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:30,000
Your ear is bleeding now.

269
00:11:30,340 --> 00:11:32,340
It's fine, that's how it is at the start.

270
00:11:32,640 --> 00:11:34,060
You're a pretty fast learner.

271
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:36,940
I guess your bloodline has a talent for it.

272
00:11:37,580 --> 00:11:40,460
It helps that the way you teach was easy for me to follow.

273
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:42,060
Go ahead to here.

274
00:11:43,020 --> 00:11:45,820
Now, before you forget what that feeling is like,

275
00:11:46,220 --> 00:11:47,140
try it on Senshi.

276
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:51,880
I'll be watching, so just go and do it like before.

277
00:11:53,160 --> 00:11:54,200
It's makeshift,

278
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:57,400
but I'm going to use some dryad branches to repair it.

279
00:11:58,040 --> 00:11:59,160
Hopefully it works.

280
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:04,740
Did it have to be there?

281
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:05,600
Oh, I...

282
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:07,500
You need to quit worrying about that!

283
00:12:07,820 --> 00:12:09,720
You can't stay shy about it!

284
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:11,960
Embarrassment's improvement's biggest enemy.

285
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:15,440
You shouldn't really disregard that sort of stuff.

286
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:18,240
Healers touch other people more than anyone,

287
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:19,700
and it can lead to some problems.

288
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:23,580
Personal relationships are the main reason parties disband.

289
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:27,960
Jealousy, envy, falling in and out of love, grudges and hate.

290
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:30,020
It's a real nuisance.

291
00:12:30,380 --> 00:12:33,460
You wouldn't happen to be talking about Fallon and Shuro.

292
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:35,280
I'm speaking from experience.

293
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:37,740
For leaders, instead of combat skills,

294
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:40,040
they should focus on keeping their team together.

295
00:12:40,040 --> 00:12:42,720
Honestly, instead of him learning magic,

296
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:46,000
I'd rather he develop good social skills and judge of character.

297
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:48,240
Because if he had those,

298
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:51,700
then he wouldn't have gotten himself in a situation involving black magic.

299
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:53,880
What about you, Chilchuk?

300
00:12:54,020 --> 00:12:55,880
Why don't you try studying some magic?

301
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:57,880
Maybe you'd stop being scared of it.

302
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:59,500
Oh, I am so sorry.

303
00:12:59,740 --> 00:13:02,420
You see, any half-foot I know who's dipped into black magic

304
00:13:02,420 --> 00:13:05,220
mysteriously got kidnapped by elves and were never seen again.

305
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:06,700
It's such a crazy coincidence.

306
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:09,360
Because of that, I've never had the chance to learn about it.

307
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:11,100
Forgive me for being so ignorant.

308
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:14,760
Actually, the ancient magic I've been researching isn't what you think.

309
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:19,020
It's magic that draws energy from a different plane where infinity exists.

310
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:22,200
How do you turn a cup that's full of water into gas?

311
00:13:22,420 --> 00:13:24,080
You simply boil it, right?

312
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:28,300
Well, then how do you turn all the water in a lake into gas?

313
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:32,620
The logic behind it's the same, but it's easier said than done.

314
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:37,100
You need magic that supports vast amounts of power and time,

315
00:13:37,460 --> 00:13:39,140
which is what coordinate magic is.

316
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:42,640
Many places in this dungeon are linked to another place.

317
00:13:43,100 --> 00:13:45,040
That power is used to summon monsters,

318
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:47,620
also to create the dungeon itself.

319
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:52,260
At that time, Valon didn't have the power to recover on her own.

320
00:13:52,260 --> 00:13:55,200
In an attempt to circumvent that,

321
00:13:55,540 --> 00:13:57,820
I ended up rewriting a section of the dungeon

322
00:13:57,820 --> 00:14:00,180
and made it so that her body was part of it.

323
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:02,220
Just for a moment, of course.

324
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:06,180
Another earthquake.

325
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:07,380
It's close.

326
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:09,640
Look over there!

327
00:14:10,260 --> 00:14:11,240
The wall's moving.

328
00:14:12,540 --> 00:14:13,620
But where's it going?

329
00:14:14,380 --> 00:14:15,660
Let's get a closer look.

330
00:14:15,660 --> 00:14:21,640
Hey, what's wrong?

331
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:23,620
I suddenly feel dizzy.

332
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:24,940
Oh, yeah, that's right!

333
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:26,960
It was your first time using magic,

334
00:14:27,180 --> 00:14:29,220
so you're likely dealing with mana sickness.

335
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:31,400
It'll hopefully ease up soon.

336
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:33,000
We'll be back.

337
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:34,100
Get rest, okay?

338
00:14:35,220 --> 00:14:37,180
Whether I open or close my eyes,

339
00:14:37,300 --> 00:14:39,000
everything looks so saturated.

340
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:46,880
Am I seeing things?

341
00:14:47,260 --> 00:14:48,420
Hearing things?

342
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:51,340
I'm begging you just for a stay.

343
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:55,000
Mana sickness really bites?

344
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:00,120
The path in front of us is changing.

345
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:02,680
I think I see a pattern.

346
00:15:03,260 --> 00:15:04,760
But then again, maybe not.

347
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:08,360
It's looking like we gotta observe things some more.

348
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:12,120
Not being able to make progress is bad, but...

349
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:12,240
Hmm?

350
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:15,620
The floor's rising all of a sudden!

351
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:16,980
Hurry and get off!

352
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:18,080
Ow!

353
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:20,020
That sure was close.

354
00:15:20,340 --> 00:15:22,340
And we almost got stuck there, huh?

355
00:15:22,340 --> 00:15:29,640
The cockatrice with merciless, petrifying venom.

356
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:36,020
Sure looks like a basilisk!

357
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:38,460
But it's a cockatrice, which is ten times more dangerous!

358
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:40,660
One bite from it, you'll turn into a statue!

359
00:15:42,040 --> 00:15:43,020
Door to the left!

360
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:44,520
Hurry and get inside!

361
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:58,340
What are we gonna do?

362
00:15:58,860 --> 00:16:00,100
This won't hold long.

363
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:02,300
Are we able to escape through the back?

364
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:05,220
If it has the same characteristics as a basilisk,

365
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:08,400
then I'm pretty sure it can detect us just by tracking our body heat.

366
00:16:09,460 --> 00:16:11,360
It'll be hard for us to sneak away.

367
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:15,260
But that's only something the snakehead has the ability to do.

368
00:16:15,680 --> 00:16:17,920
The birdhead's relying on sight to find us.

369
00:16:18,700 --> 00:16:23,000
Marcil, do you remember what Laios did when we faced a basilisk the last time?

370
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:29,380
Whatever you do, don't back down.

371
00:16:29,740 --> 00:16:32,300
Put your whole body and soul into intimidating it.

372
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:35,320
That's easy for you to say.

373
00:16:35,720 --> 00:16:37,840
All you gotta do is make yourself look big,

374
00:16:38,020 --> 00:16:39,780
and yell at it nice and strong!

375
00:16:39,780 --> 00:16:42,720
I get that I'm taller than Chilchuk and Senshi,

376
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:46,300
but this monster's twice the size of a basilisk,

377
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:48,540
and I'm honestly not that good at yelling.

378
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:52,140
Wait, what did Laios yell back then?

379
00:16:52,860 --> 00:16:53,660
Was it...

380
00:16:53,660 --> 00:16:55,680
Or...

381
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:57,440
Maybe...

382
00:16:57,440 --> 00:17:02,620
Well, regardless of what it was,

383
00:17:02,840 --> 00:17:04,500
I've just gotta make it flinch!

384
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:10,940
Roll credits.

385
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:12,620
What am I even doing?

386
00:17:12,840 --> 00:17:14,580
I'm definitely gonna screw it up!

387
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:16,640
I can't do what Laios does!

388
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:18,320
How am I supposed to do this?

389
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:20,820
I know.

390
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:22,780
I'll do it...

391
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:24,860
My own way!

392
00:17:24,860 --> 00:17:30,960
The magic school's first-ever genius,

393
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:32,080
Marcel!

394
00:17:35,320 --> 00:17:36,820
What was that explosion?

395
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:37,620
It's Marcel!

396
00:17:38,060 --> 00:17:38,500
Come on!

397
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:46,560
Too shallow!

398
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:50,460
Crap, I made too much noise!

399
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:52,560
Both heads are looking at me now!

400
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:54,100
They need to cast,

401
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:55,340
but there's no time...

402
00:17:55,340 --> 00:18:06,340
Marcel!

403
00:18:06,900 --> 00:18:07,980
Did you get bitten?

404
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:09,620
I'm okay.

405
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:13,780
That looks like a bite to me, you idiot!

406
00:18:14,480 --> 00:18:15,200
Damn it!

407
00:18:15,620 --> 00:18:16,080
What?

408
00:18:16,300 --> 00:18:18,020
You got bitten by a cockatrice?

409
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:19,180
This is bad.

410
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:22,000
Do you know the trick to help you deal with a cockatrice bite?

411
00:18:22,700 --> 00:18:24,160
There's a trick to it?

412
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:25,900
First, remove your pants.

413
00:18:27,220 --> 00:18:29,340
Sit and bring your body close together.

414
00:18:31,040 --> 00:18:32,400
Pull your arms inward.

415
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:34,180
Cover your ears with your fingers.

416
00:18:34,620 --> 00:18:35,560
And close your mouth.

417
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:39,480
Good.

418
00:18:39,800 --> 00:18:41,480
Now you're all set to turn into stone.

419
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:45,160
I thought this was a method not to get petrified, you little...

420
00:18:46,380 --> 00:18:50,900
Oh, crap.

421
00:18:50,900 --> 00:18:53,300
She got hardened in a really dangerous pose.

422
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:54,300
She's gonna break.

423
00:18:54,420 --> 00:18:57,220
Her core is unbalanced, so she could tip over any second.

424
00:18:57,720 --> 00:18:59,040
Not looking good.

425
00:18:59,860 --> 00:19:02,040
Of all the poses she could have chosen.

426
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:03,920
What should we do now?

427
00:19:04,280 --> 00:19:05,940
Is there any way to undo this?

428
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:08,380
There's a few ways.

429
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:10,700
First is waiting till it just wears off.

430
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:14,340
Petrification's more like a curse instead of a poison.

431
00:19:14,980 --> 00:19:16,840
Elves have a strong resistance to magic,

432
00:19:16,840 --> 00:19:19,140
so they should recover faster than others.

433
00:19:20,060 --> 00:19:22,760
The second way is to search for some medicinal herbs.

434
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:26,380
Or third, to go look for an adventurer who knows the right spell.

435
00:19:27,140 --> 00:19:30,640
Last option is to let me try to cast something to heal her.

436
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:32,300
Can you, though?

437
00:19:32,300 --> 00:19:35,400
Marcel taught me the basics of reading her magic book.

438
00:19:36,020 --> 00:19:37,980
There should be a spell to get her back to normal.

439
00:19:40,560 --> 00:19:43,060
Well, while looking for herbs and an adventurer,

440
00:19:43,320 --> 00:19:45,460
I'll stay hopeful about the other two ideas.

441
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:48,320
So, how long would it take to heal up naturally?

442
00:19:49,320 --> 00:19:51,560
For Tallman, it's six months to ten years.

443
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:53,940
I'm gonna fetch the cockatrice.

444
00:19:56,940 --> 00:19:59,260
These changed color real fast overnight.

445
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:01,360
We should eat them sooner than later.

446
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:04,180
She's leaning, and it's kind of concerning.

447
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:07,400
Should we put something underneath her butt to keep her up straight?

448
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:09,100
Yeah, that might help.

449
00:20:09,340 --> 00:20:10,620
I've got a pretty good idea.

450
00:20:11,280 --> 00:20:12,640
At the bottom of the pan,

451
00:20:12,780 --> 00:20:15,040
place the julienned flower buds and some spices.

452
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:17,560
And place Marcel on top of that.

453
00:20:18,780 --> 00:20:20,800
Oh, her eyelashes broke.

454
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:22,620
Soak the cockatrice meat in a brine

455
00:20:22,620 --> 00:20:24,360
and place that in Marcel's lap.

456
00:20:24,720 --> 00:20:27,060
And this way, she stays perfectly balanced.

457
00:20:29,680 --> 00:20:31,760
Well, she does seem more stable.

458
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:34,040
This should keep her from taking a tumble.

459
00:20:34,760 --> 00:20:36,900
She looks kind of like a heretic idol.

460
00:20:37,580 --> 00:20:38,740
From that point on,

461
00:20:38,840 --> 00:20:40,560
Laios and the others worked hard.

462
00:20:41,560 --> 00:20:43,520
There were many trials and errors.

463
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:47,120
But on the fourth day...

464
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:47,920
They found one!

465
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:50,100
How do you reckon you use it?

466
00:20:50,100 --> 00:20:54,700
Uh, how about we stick him on?

467
00:20:55,660 --> 00:20:57,580
The stone is starting to feel a little warm.

468
00:20:58,400 --> 00:20:59,240
Now's the time.

469
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:08,440
Am I even pronouncing any of this correctly?

470
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:09,080
Crap!

471
00:21:18,760 --> 00:21:19,860
Marcel, you're back!

472
00:21:19,920 --> 00:21:20,840
Yep, soft.

473
00:21:21,140 --> 00:21:22,340
I said the word's right!

474
00:21:22,820 --> 00:21:23,600
Wait, huh?

475
00:21:23,940 --> 00:21:24,920
What the...

476
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:26,360
Is this a vegetable?

477
00:21:26,820 --> 00:21:28,020
Why is there a pot?

478
00:21:28,600 --> 00:21:29,800
Let's see here.

479
00:21:30,320 --> 00:21:30,580
Hmm.

480
00:21:31,120 --> 00:21:32,840
This one was a success, too!

481
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:33,340
Yay!

482
00:21:33,340 --> 00:21:37,800
Boil the meat that you had brine in, and then slice it up thinly.

483
00:21:38,520 --> 00:21:42,820
Take the fermented buds, plate them with the meat, and it's ready.

484
00:21:42,820 --> 00:21:45,740
What?

485
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:47,540
It's really been that long?

486
00:21:47,980 --> 00:21:50,380
I wonder what method ended up working in the end.

487
00:21:50,660 --> 00:21:52,720
No way to tell when we tried so many.

488
00:21:53,140 --> 00:21:55,340
It'd be nice if it was the spell I cast.

489
00:21:55,580 --> 00:21:56,460
Yeah, right.

490
00:21:56,600 --> 00:21:58,680
It was probably all thanks to the herb I found.

491
00:21:58,680 --> 00:21:59,420
You sure?

492
00:21:59,920 --> 00:22:03,540
Because maybe their cockatries mean I was prepping somehow neutralize the curse.

493
00:22:03,540 --> 00:22:08,860
I caused them so much trouble, and at a time when we really needed to get back to the surface.

494
00:22:09,620 --> 00:22:10,760
Hey, guys, I...

495
00:22:10,760 --> 00:22:12,740
No, wait a second.

496
00:22:13,500 --> 00:22:16,780
Under the circumstances, there's something I should tell them first.

497
00:22:17,580 --> 00:22:18,680
Yeah, of course.

498
00:22:20,240 --> 00:22:22,900
Don't ever use people as a human pickling weight.

499
00:22:23,980 --> 00:22:28,420
So it goes with dungeon food delicious in dungeon.

